// How the page that explains the app is served. Its own name and its own
// deployment, sharing nothing with the app next door — which is the same
// separation the rest of this directory keeps.
//
// The worker keeps the name it was created under, from when this directory was
// docs/ and the site answered on docs.choai.dev: the dashboard's build is tied
// to it, and renaming it here would deploy a new worker beside the old one.
{
  "name": "choai-docs",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-15",
  // It answers on choai.dev, attached where the deployment is rather than
  // declared here, for the reason README gives beside the app's own name. The
  // workers.dev address is left on, so there is somewhere to look at a build
  // that has not been given a name yet. docs.choai.dev, where it used to
  // answer, is sent here by a redirect rule on the zone rather than by this
  // worker — README says which.
  "assets": {
    // Astro writes each page as a directory, and the default handling answers
    // both spellings of a path, which is what astro.config.mjs asks for. There
    // is no single page to fall back to and no 404 page to serve, so a path
    // that is not a page is a 404 and says so.
    "directory": "./dist"
  }
}
